ce": "1894, David Storrar Meldrum, The Story of Margrédel: Being a Fireside History of a Fifeshire Family, page 228:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(informal, intransitive) To lift weights; to weight-lift.", "tags": ["informal", "intransitive"], "examples": ["She lifts twice a week at the gym."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To try to raise something; to exert the strength for raising or bearing.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "strained by lifting at a weight too heavy", "reference": "a. 1705, John Locke, “Of the Conduct of the Understanding”, in Posthumous Works of Mr. John Locke: […], London: […] A[wnsham] and J[ohn] Churchill, […], published 1706, →OCLC:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "nostaa"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "To elevate or improve in rank, condition, etc.; often with up.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The Roman virtues lift up mortal man.", "reference": "1712 (date written), [Joseph] Addison, Cato, a Tragedy. […], London: […] J[acob] Tonson, […], published 1713, →OCLC, Act I, scene iv, page 9:"}, {"text": "being lifted up with pride", "reference": "1611, The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], →OCLC, 1 Timothy 3:6:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "rütbəcə yüksəltmək"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "qabağa çəkmək"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "irəli çəkmək"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "irəli çəkmək"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "rütbəcə yüksəltmək"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "povýšit"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"},